        "answer": "**Coverage note:** The knowledge base covers Barclays reports from **June 12 to September 29, 2025**, not the full calendar year.\n\n| Report date | NVDA price target | Prior target | Change | Rating |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| Jun. 17, 2025 | **$200** | $170 | **+18%** | Overweight, unchanged [Barclays, 2025-06-17, p.1] |\n| Aug. 13, 2025 | No NVDA target update—the report was a broader AI-power thematic note [Barclays, 2025-08-13, p.1] |\n| Sep. 25, 2025 | **$240** | $200 | **+20%** | Overweight, unchanged [Barclays, 2025-09-25, p.1] |\n\nBarclays therefore moved its NVDA target from **$170 before the June report to $200 in June and $240 in September**. That is a cumulative **$70, or roughly 41%, increase**, while retaining its **Overweight** rating. The June increase reflected confidence in second-half Blackwell-related upside; the September increase followed Barclays’ estimate of more than **$2 trillion** in planned AI infrastructure spending, much of which it expected to flow through NVDA’s P&L [Barclays, 2025-06-17, p.1] [Barclays, 2025-09-25, p.1].",
